  "worked_solution": "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\u03ba(s)=\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(s)\u2016\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=5\\pi $: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{\u2032}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{5})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5}))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5}))\\,k \\\\  & =(0)\\,i-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,k \\\\ {T}^{\u2032}(5\\pi ) & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\cdot (5\\pi )}{5})\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\cdot (5\\pi )}{5})\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\pi )\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (-1)\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (0)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03ba(5\\pi ) & =\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(5\\pi )\u2016 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
